            <div class="container" style="padding-left:2%;max-width:100%">
                <div class="row">

                    <div class="col-md-12">

                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-3 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;max-width:100%">


                            <h5 style="color:orange">Course Highlights</h5>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2">
                                A comprehensive Microsoft SQL Server course typically transitions from foundational database concepts to advanced enterprise management.
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2">

                                <ul>

                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>
                                            T-SQL Fundamentals & Querying
                                        </b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Data Retrieval</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Mastering the SELECT statement, filtering with WHERE, and sorting with ORDER BY.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Data Manipulation (DML)</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                       Learning to INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE records while maintaining data integrity.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Advanced Querying</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Using complex JOIN operations (Inner, Outer, Self), subqueries, and Common Table Expressions (CTEs) to combine data from multiple tables
                                                    </p>
                                                    
                                                </li>
                                               
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Database Design & Development</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Schema Design</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Applying normalization (1NF to 3NF) to minimize redundancy and ensure efficient data structures.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Programmability</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Creating and managing Stored Procedures, User-Defined Functions (UDFs), and Triggers to encapsulate business logic
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Constraints</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Implementing Primary Keys, Foreign Keys, and Unique constraints to enforce data rules.
                                                    </p>

                                                </li>
                                                 
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Administration & Performance Tuning</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Performance Optimization</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Analyzing Execution Plans and implementing indexing strategies (Clustered vs. Non-Clustered) to speed up queries.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Maintenance & Security</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Configuring backup/restore protocols, managing user roles/permissions, and applying encryption (TDE).
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>High Availability</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Exploring Always On Availability Groups and failover clustering for disaster recovery.
                                                    </p>

                                                </li>

                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>
                                            Business Intelligence & Modern Features
                                        </b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            <ul>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>The BI Stack</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Introductory modules on Integration Services (SSIS) for ETL, Analysis Services (SSAS) for OLAP, and Reporting Services (SSRS).
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                                <li>
                                                    <b>Cloud & AI Integration</b>
                                                    <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                                        Working with Azure SQL Database and new SQL Server 2025 features like Vector Search for AI applications.
                                                    </p>
                                                </li>
                                            </ul>
                                        </div>

                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>



                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-5 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;margin-top:2% ;max-width:100%">

                            <h5 style="color:orange">
                                Who can do?
                            </h5>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                Microsoft SQL Server is accessible to a wide range of individuals, from complete beginners to seasoned IT professionals. Because it uses a declarative language (T-SQL) that closely resembles English, the barrier to entry is relatively low compared to other programming languages
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Fresh Graduates & Students</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Ideal for those starting a career in data, IT, or business. Many entry-level courses require no prior database experience.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>IT Professionals</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                             System administrators, support engineers, or developers looking to upskill or transition into database administration (DBA) or data engineering roles.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Non-Technical Professionals</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            "Power users" in fields like marketing, sales, and finance. Learning SQL helps these professionals perform self-service data analysis without relying on IT teams.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Career Switchers</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Individuals from unrelated backgrounds (e.g., retail, hospitality) can use SQL as a gateway into the tech industry due to its high demand and structured learning paths.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
